摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Unofficial Windows and macOS desktop app for DeepSeek Harness, with bundled runtime and automatic reuse of existing DSH environments.","id":"gh:1334946785","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-desktop","slug":"yxccai/dsh-desktop","topics":["deepdeepseek","deepseek-harness","desktop","desktop-app","dsh","dsh-desktop","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-desktop","dsh-plugins","sider"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Unofficial Windows and macOS desktop app for DeepSeek Harness, with bundled runtime and automatic re"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"use of existing DSH environments."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Desktop"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"An unofficial open-source desktop app for DeepSeek Harness, designed to provide a simpler and more c"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"onvenient desktop experience."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### A desktop shell around the official DSH Web — inherited features, secure, and easy to keep curre"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"# A desktop shell around the official DSH Web — inherited features, secure, and easy to keep current"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"DSH Desktop does not reimplement any functionality; it wraps the official DSH Web in a native deskto"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"op does not reimplement any functionality; it wraps the official DSH Web in a native desktop window:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **One-click launch**: No browser tab, no URL, no command line — double-click the desktop icon to e"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"nter the same runtime environment as the official Web.\n- **Feature inheritance**: The official DSH W"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"eb serves as the host runtime, loading its full UI and plugin system while sessions, workspace data,"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" and the plugin ecosystem are fully preserved; the Web plugin market component among the built-in pl"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"ugins manages plugins for both the desktop and the Web version from a single place.\n- **Safe isolati"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"on**: The renderer never receives direct Node.js, filesystem, or arbitrary command access; the Elect"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"ron sandbox, contextIsolation, loopback-only navigation, and a whitelisted IPC layer form the isolat"},{"id":"p8s8","text":"ion boundary.\n- **Simple upgrades**: When the official DSH ships a new version, the desktop updates "},{"id":"p8s9","text":"with a version bump and a rebuilt bundle. Existing `DSH_HOME`, sessions, Agent Presets, and persiste"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"nt plugins carry over unchanged."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Foundation stays lean — only a few practical desktop enhancements"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The base build does not pile on features; it keeps the official Web experience and adds only the enh"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ancements most useful in a desktop context:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **Project panel**: Beside the chat, it lists the files actually modified or produced by each reply"},{"id":"p11s2","text":". Multi-tab previews cover Markdown, HTML, source code, diff, CSV, PDF, images, and text, with split"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" editing and conflict-aware atomic saves. Git workspaces show real status and per-file discard; non-"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"Git directories use content snapshots (no `git init`, nothing written into the project). Each reply "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"records a recoverable snapshot, and restoring always saves the current state as a recovery point fir"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"st.\n- **Built-in plugins (optional install)**: Built-ins are offered as a selectable catalog rather "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"than pre-installed. Available now: multiple color themes (Deep Ocean Blue, Aurora Green-Purple, Rose"},{"id":"p11s8","text":" Sunset Pink, Warm Sand Amber, each with light and dark modes), a custom image background (native fi"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"le picker, adjustable opacity, instant disable), and a lightweight writing assistant (drafting, rewr"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"iting, summarizing, translating). All support install, disable, and uninstall on demand.\n- **Windows"},{"id":"p11s11","text":" system notifications (optional)**: Get a native notification when the agent awaits approval, finish"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"es a task, or stops with an error — no need to watch the page constantly. Toggle it anytime under Se"},{"id":"p11s13","text":"ttings → Plugins → Built-in Plugins; off by default."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Extensible and creative — a complete plugin ecosystem on a lean base"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The base stays light; extension capabilities are directly available:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **Built-in plugins keep growing**: Official curated plugins ship through a trusted channel with in"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"tegrity verification, and can be installed, disabled, or uninstalled without touching user content.\n"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"- **Community plugin market**: A fixed, verified copy of the community market component is included."},{"id":"p14s4","text":" Once enabled, Settings → Plugins → Plugin Market browses awesome-dsh-plugin.com — install, update, "},{"id":"p14s5","text":"and uninstall community plugins centrally, with a bundled `pnpm` so nothing needs to be installed gl"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"obally. Installs go into the shared `DSH_HOME` and work in both the desktop and the browser version."},{"id":"p14s7","text":"\n- **Scale on demand**: Add capabilities from the built-in and community catalogs when needed; keep "},{"id":"p14s8","text":"the base experience lean when not."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Download"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Two ways to use"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Way | For whom | What you get |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| **One-click installer** | Most users | Double-click to install and run; no environment needed. You"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"r own data is used (`DSH_HOME`, sessions, plugins), but DSH is started by the desktop's bundled runt"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ime |\n| **Connect mode** | Users with Node.js who want the full official DSH | Not just your data — "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"the DSH Web itself is also started by you with the system Node (npx pulls the latest release); the d"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"esktop only connects as a shell and never uses the bundled runtime |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Both ways share the same data (`DSH_HOME`, sessions, plugins) and can be switched freely. Developers"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" can also run from source; `npm start` uses `auto` mode and prefers the system environment."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### One-click installer"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Download from GitHub Releases:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- Windows x64 Setup\n- SHA-256 checksums"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### macOS (test build)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Apple Silicon (M-series):"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- macOS arm64 DMG\n- macOS arm64 ZIP"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The Intel (x64) build appears on the Releases page once the runner finishes."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"On first launch, Control-click the app in Finder and choose **Open**. If macOS still blocks it, go t"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"o **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway**. Signing and notarization are planned for a"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ngs → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway**. Signing and notarization are planned for a future release."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### Conversation-aware project panel"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Conversation snapshots and per-file rollback"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Managed Plugin Center"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"### Community plugin market"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"After the bundled community market component is mounted into the shared `DSH_HOME`, it manages plugi"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"ns already installed on both the desktop and the Web side, and lets you browse and install newly add"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"ed community plugins at any time:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"DSH Desktop automatically selects an available runtime:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"1. Connect to an existing DSH service.\n2. Reuse a global `dsh` installation.\n3. Reuse the system `np"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"x/npm` environment.\n4. Fall back to the bundled DSH runtime."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Existing users can usually keep their original `DSH_HOME`, sessions, Agent Presets, and persistent p"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"lugins. New users do not need to install DSH or Node.js first."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## Plugin compatibility"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Plugins built on official DSH/Cordis services, Host tools, UI slots, themes, and persistent Presets "},{"id":"p39s2","text":"generally offer the best compatibility. Plugins that depend on fixed DOM structures, browser extensi"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"ons, or development HMR require separate testing."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
